      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start for a general summary, but I'm worried that if we're too vague about the 5% vs the 20% target, they'll catch the discrepancy during due diligence and reject us for being dishonest. \n\nCan we be more assertive with the actual wording in that section? I want the narrative to really lean into the success of the project so they don't even see the 5% as a failure. How can we write this so it reads like a major win that proves we're the best choice for this $5M?",
